  "notes": [
    "test = held-out PlantVillage split: lab photos on plain backgrounds. Only part of it has verified leaf grouping; compare test_leaf_verified_only with test_fallback_grouping_only.",
    "field = PlantDoc's official TEST photos mapped onto our classes (plus any local photos), minus near-duplicates of training photos. No run trained on them. Labels are the dataset authors' own. Mappings marked approximate are in 'field' but not in 'field_exact_mapping_only'. Classes with fewer images than the minimum are not scored.",
    "*_crop_known = the same images, but with the classes of every other crop switched off, as if the user had picked the crop first. It measures the app design, not the model alone.",
    "unknown = leaves of other crops (plus any local non-leaf photos). Without photos of hands, soil or objects in data/nonleaf, the threshold is only tested against other plants' leaves.",
    "Confidence intervals resample images as if independent. Several photos of one leaf are correlated, so the real uncertainty is larger.",
    "Temperature is fitted on lab validation (plus field validation for runs trained on field photos; see temperature_fitted_on). The threshold is chosen on one half of the unknown images (split by file hash) and reported on the other half.",
    "The field test set is small (check n_images and classes_below_min_support). Differences of a few points between runs are inside the confidence intervals."
  ]
